{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786890530181,"sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_00_LYtxzQPyntrvsY91FgYz5628","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"smart-routing","path":".opencode/skills/sk-doc","include":"*.md"},"output":"Found 26 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.0.1.0.md:\n  Line 3: description: \"Root ROUTER.md adoption: the hub's second-stage surface router moves from shared/references/smart-routing.md to a first-class root ROUTER.md with router_state: active, the machine block preserved byte-for-byte, and the stage-one default left untouched.\"\n\n  Line 34: - `shared/references/smart-routing.md` after standalone contract validation. The parent doctor then passed; compiled-manifest freshness remains the downstream fleet-rebuild gate.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md:\n  Line 3: description: First-class surface router document at the sk-doc hub root (ROUTER.md). hub-router.json selects the workflow mode; this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local leaf resources that mode should load, emitting canonical (workflowMode, leafResourceId) pairs. Relocated verbatim from shared/references/smart-routing.md (v1.0.0.0) as the ROUTER.md consolidation pattern.\n\n  Line 218:         \"sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md\",\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/manual-testing-playbook/token-cost-baseline/max-load.md:\n  Line 106:   - sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md\n\n  Line 324:     leaf_resource_id: assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md\n\n  Line 370:     leaf_resource_id: assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-changelog/changelog/v1.0.1.0.md:\n  Line 14: - **Section contract conformance** -- The opening `SKILL.md` heading combined when-to-use guidance and routing under one merged title, and the routing token used an underscore, so the shared section contract could not match a standalone smart-routing section. This splits the opening into a `WHEN TO USE` section and a `SMART ROUTING` section, keeping every existing activation trigger, exclusion, and family-boundary note, and adds an explicit output-mode routing summary that points at the detailed workflow sections.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/benchmark/reports/compiled-routing/2026-07-21--benchmark-sweep--r3/hub-reports/sk-code.md:\n  Line 43: | SD-001 | ok | MISMATCH | intent: —<br>resources: references/stack-detection.md<br>references/smart-routing.md<br>references/phase-detection.md<br>references/universal/code-quality-standards.md<br>code-webflow/references/implementation/webflow-patterns/overview-limits-and-collection-lists.md<br>code-webflow/references/implementation/animation-workflows/overview-decision-tree-and-css.md<br>code-webflow/references/implementation/observer-patterns/mutation-and-intersection.md<br>code-webflow/references/javascript/quality-standards/init-dom-error-and-async.md<br>code-webflow/references/javascript/style-guide/overview-naming-and-structure.md<br>code-webflow/references/css/style-guide.md<br>code-webflow/references/shared/cross-language-rules.md | intent: code-webflow<br>resources: references/stack-detection.md<br>references/phase-detection.md<br>references/smart-routing.md<br>references/universal/code-quality-standards.md<br>