{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786890535071,"sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_01_7fzYEX3JtG4V4WECr06J5909","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"smart-routing","path":".opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill"},"output":"Found 13 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-smart-router.md:\n  Line 166: - **Path contract (nested packets):** inside a parent hub that explicitly declares a second-layer surface router, a packet's `references/`/`assets/` paths become packet-qualified `leafResourceId`s in that router. A raw path converts to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at exactly one boundary — the leaf-resource contract — via a packet-qualified prefix or an authored shared alias, never by generic prefix stripping. Workflow-only hubs such as `sk-doc` do not need this second layer. See [parent-hub-router-schema.md](../../references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md) §8 and scaffold the surface router from [parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md](../parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md) only when the hub contract calls for it.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md:\n  Line 29: Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path is either packet-qualified (`[packet]/references|assets/…`) or a shared-alias disk path (`shared/…` listed in `leaf-aliases.json`). Both convert to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the one contract boundary. Keep `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` keys aligned. Delete `FULL_INVENTORY` if the hub has no show-everything intent. A root `skill_pointer: SKILL.md` and a four-part `version` are required in both states, and the router must never coexist with a legacy `smart-routing.md`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-router-template.json:\n  Line 5:   \"_defaultResourceNote\": \"The hub-router.json defaultResource is a stage-one fallback and is never required to name ROUTER.md. It is only rejected when it literally names a legacy smart-routing path; preserve each hub's existing zero-signal fallback semantics.\",\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md:\n  Line 306: - [`parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md`](./parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md) - the root `ROUTER.md` stage-two authoring template.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md:\n  Line 134: Stage one and stage two are separate authoring acts. `hub-router.json` selects a workflow mode. The root `ROUTER.md` then owns stage-two leaf selection when `active` — mapping request intent to the exact packet-local leaf resources that mode loads — or declares `stage1-only` and leaves the whole routing story to stage one. A fresh hub scaffolds `stage1-only` with empty maps, a root `SKILL.md` pointer, and a four-part `version`. Promotion to `active` is the deliberate act of authoring non-empty equal-key maps with resolvable, typed leaf paths; the authoring tooling never fabricates those maps. See [`parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md`](../../assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md) for both states.\n\n  Line 247: - [parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md](../../assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md) - root `ROUTER.md` stage-two authoring template.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md:\n  Line 315: The hub router selects a **mode**; it emits packet pointers, not the per-intent leaf gold. The exact leaf resources an intent should load belong in the root `ROUTER.md`, scaffolded from [`parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md`](../../assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md).\n\n  Line 346: - [parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md](../../assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md) - the root `ROUTER.md` stage-two authoring template (active and stage1-only states).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/root-router-contract.cjs:\n  Line 74:   'shared/references/smart-routing.md',\n\n  Line 75:   'references/smart-routing.md',\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/root-router-contract.test.cjs:\n  Line 313:     legacyFiles: ['shared/references/smart-routing.md'],\n\n  Line 405:     hubRouterDefaultResource: ['shared/references/smart-routing.md', 'mode-registry.json'],\n\n  Line 415:       defaults: '[\"references/smart-routing.md\"]',\n","metadata":{"matches":13,"truncated":false},"title":"smart-routing","time":{"start":1786890535050,"end":1786890535070}},"id":"prt_00af9bfe1001b9RLwKlUdQJKZR","sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","messageID":"msg_00af9b171001zd3qGRhjhCdDRa"}}
