{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786890725898,"sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_00_A4dMMwV8YjHOgE7e0Rir1510","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs","pattern":"ROUTER\\.md|router_state|smart-routing|root-router|smart-router"},"output":"Found 65 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/root-router-contract.cjs:\n  Line 2: // ║ root-router-contract — two-state root ROUTER.md contract                 ║\n\n  Line 7:  * root-router-contract.cjs — pure validator for the two-state root ROUTER.md\n\n  Line 10:  * Every parent hub owns one root control document, ROUTER.md, that declares\n\n  Line 31:  * defaultResource needs no ROUTER.md entry — it is only ever rejected when it\n\n  Line 32:  * literally names a legacy smart-router path.\n\n  Line 49:  * No filesystem access happens here. Callers own reading the ROUTER.md,\n\n  Line 70:  * Root ROUTER.md must not coexist with either one (dual-source ambiguity), and\n\n  Line 74:   'shared/references/smart-routing.md',\n\n  Line 75:   'references/smart-routing.md',\n\n  Line 199:  * @param {string} text - The whole ROUTER.md text.\n\n  Line 350:  * smart-router path. Zero-signal fallback semantics are otherwise untouched:\n\n  Line 351:  * nothing here requires or forbids a default pointing at ROUTER.md.\n\n  Line 365:       message: `a live default resource literally names a legacy smart-router path: ${offending.join(', ')}`,\n\n  Line 371:  * Validate one root ROUTER.md against the two-state contract.\n\n  Line 374:  * @param {string|null} [args.routerText] - ROUTER.md file contents, or null when the file is missing.\n\n  Line 383:  *   router_state when it was well-formed, else null.\n\n  Line 404:       message: 'no root ROUTER.md at the hub root',\n\n  Line 416:       message: `root ROUTER.md coexists with legacy router file(s): ${legacyFiles.join(', ')}`,\n\n  Line 422:   const stateValues = frontmatterValues(frontmatter, 'router_state');\n\n  Line 426:       message: 'router_state is absent from the ROUTER.md frontmatter (must be active or stage1-only)',\n\n  Line 431:       message: `router_state is declared more than once: ${stateValues.join(', ')}`,\n\n  Line 436:       message: `router_state ${JSON.stringify(stateValues[0])} is not one of ${VALID_STATES.join(', ')}`,\n\n  Line 443:   // version is part of the same machine-declaration block as router_state, so\n\n  Line 450:       message: 'version is absent from the ROUTER.md frontmatter (must be a four-part numeric version like 1.0.0.0)',\n\n  Line 475:       message: `skill_pointer is absent from the ROUTER.md frontmatter (must be exactly ${JSON.stringify(ROOT_POINTER)})`,\n\n  Line 661:         message: `stage1-only ROUTER.md must keep stage-two collections declared and empty: ${unreadable.join('; ')}`,\n\n  Line 677:         message: `stage1-only ROUTER.md must keep stage-two collections empty but declares: ${offending.join(', ')}`,\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/README.md:\n  Line 26: | `root-router-contract.cjs` | Validates the two-state root ROUTER.md contract (active / stage1-only) with stable negative codes. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/root-router-contract.test.cjs:\n  Line 3: // ║ root-router-contract.test — coverage for the two-state ROUTER.md contract ║\n\n  Line 8:  * Covers the root-router contract library end to end: every positive shape\n\n  Line 21: const routerContract = require('../lib/root-router-contract.cjs');\n\n  Line 57:  * Build a ROUTER.md document from a state and explicit machine collections.\n\n  Line 69:   frontmatterLines.push(`router_state: ${state}`, `skill_pointer: ${pointer}`, '---');\n\n  Line 220:   'router_state: stage1-only',\n\n  Line 248:     'router_state: active',\n\n  Line 290:   const text = routerText('active').replace(/router_state: active\\n/, '');\n\n  Line 296:   const text = routerText('active').replace('router_state: active', 'router_state: beta-only');\n\n  Line 303:     'router_state: active',\n\n  Line 304:     'router_state: active\\nrouter_state: stage1-only',\n\n  Line 313:     legacyFiles: ['shared/references/smart-routing.md'],\n\n  Line 405:     hubRouterDefaultResource: ['shared/references/smart-routing.md', 'mode-registry.json'],\n\n  Line 415:       defaults: '[\"references/smart-routing.md\"]',\n\n  Line 428:       resources: '{\\n    \"ALPHA\": [\"ROUTER.md\"],\\n}',\n\n  Line 497: // The version is part of the same declaration block as router_state: exactly\n\n  Line 673: console.log('[root-router-contract] all positive and negative fixtures passed');\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/README.md:\n  Line 27: | `root-router-contract.test.cjs` | Tests the two-state root ROUTER.md contract and its stable negative codes. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/create-journey-proof.test.cjs:\n  Line 25: const ROOT_ROUTER_CONTRACT_PATH = path.join(REPO_ROOT, '.opencode', 'skills', 'sk-doc', 'sk-create-skill', 'scripts', 'lib', 'root-router-contract.cjs');\n\n  Line 78:   fs.copyFileSync(ROOT_ROUTER_CONTRACT_PATH, path.join(libDir, 'root-router-contract.cjs'));\n\n  Line 102:   // ROUTER.md: empty stage-two collections, a root SKILL.md pointer, and a\n\n  Line 104:   const routerPath = path.join(tempRoot, 'proof-hub', 'ROUTER.md');\n\n  Line 105:   assert.ok(fs.existsSync(routerPath), 'fresh parent scaffold must ship a root ROUTER.md');\n\n  Line 107:   assert.match(routerSource, /router_state: stage1-only/);\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/package_skill.py:\n  Line 172: # smart-router markers, placeholder/TODO completeness). Recommended-section, file-type,\n\n  Line 182:     \"missing smart-router marker\",    # SMART ROUTING resilience markers\n\n  Line 330:     section / RULES / smart-router shape checks and the description soft-target\n\n  Line 644:     Checks for the canonical smart-router resilience markers\n\n  Line 684:             f\"SMART ROUTING section missing smart-router marker(s): \"\n\n  Line 791:     # smart-router markers. Emitted as warnings (see VERSIONED_DOC_SUBTREES\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/init_skill.py:\n  Line 463:     \"\"\"Return the stage1-only root ROUTER.md a fresh parent hub is born with.\n\n  Line 467:     and the document declares `router_state: stage1-only`, delegating all\n\n  Line 484:         'router_state: stage1-only\\n'\n\n  Line 491:         '`ROUTER.md`. The hub selects a workflow mode in [`hub-router.json`](hub-router.json);\\n'\n\n  Line 493:         'declares `router_state: stage1-only`, so it owns no second-stage leaf selection:\\n'\n\n  Line 512:         'Replace `router_state: stage1-only` with `router_state: active` only after\\n'\n\n  Line 737:         (skill_dir / 'ROUTER.md').write_text(router_content, encoding='utf-8')\n","metadata":{"matches":65,"truncated":false},"title":"ROUTER\\.md|router_state|smart-routing|root-router|smart-router","time":{"start":1786890725883,"end":1786890725897}},"id":"prt_00afca8ae001SE0yvgUdnjqZVw","sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMN