{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786890752998,"sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_xvWTdkbRJItAOFro8hJ98559","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: RUNTIME MIRROR PARITY (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator reporting whether every runtime config dir still mirrors its canonical source\n5: purpose: Detect drift across the agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors that .claude, .codex, .cursor and .devin derive from .opencode\n6: action: Run the five mirror checkers -> aggregate their verdicts -> report per-surface drift\n7: skill_owner: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single-step\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"Every checker below is invoked in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT run any generator in write mode, create or delete a symlink, or install a hook config. Repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of a diagnostic.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   runtime_mirrors: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"\n35:   codex_agents: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/codex/sync-agents.cjs\"\n36:   codex_prompts: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\"\n37:   agent_roster: \".opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/agent-roster-mirror-check.cjs\"\n38:   codex_hooks_installer: \".opencode/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\"\n39:   pi_agents: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\"\n40:   pi_prompts: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\"\n41: \n42: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n43: # INPUTS\n44: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n45: inputs:\n46:   none: \"This diagnostic takes no arguments. Every checker derives its expected state from the canonical trees and the runtimes' own config files.\"\n47: \n48: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: # EXECUTION\n50: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n51: execution:\n52:   steps:\n53:     - \"Run upstream_assets.runtime_mirrors with --check. Covers the cursor/devin agent, command and skill symlink trees plus all four hook discovery mirrors. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n54:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_agents with --check. Covers the generated .codex/agents/*.toml. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n55:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .codex/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n56:     - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_roster. Covers roster coverage across all five surfaces and rejects a real file where a symlink belongs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = canonical dir missing.\"\n57:     - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_hooks_installer with --check. Covers the user-global ~/.codex/hooks.json against the repo's .codex/hooks.json, including orphaned entries whose .opencode adapter no longer exists on disk. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n58:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_agents with --check. Covers the generated .pi/agents/*.md. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n59:     - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .pi/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n60:     - \"Aggregate: report each surface with its own verdict rather than a single pass/fail, so the operator learns which mirror moved.\"\n61: \n62: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n63: # OUTPUT\n64: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n65: output: |\n66:   STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync.\n67:   STATUS=DRIFT when any checker reports drift, listing each drifting surface and the repair command for it:\n68:     runtime mirrors  -> node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n69:     codex agents     -> node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/codex/sync-agents.cjs\n70:     codex prompts    -> node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\n71:     codex hooks      -> node .opencode/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\n72:     pi agents        -> node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\n73:     pi prompts       -> node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\n74:   The agent roster check has no generator; its drift is repaired by the runtime-mirrors generator or by hand\n75:   for the authored surfaces (.opencode/agents, .codex/agents).\n76:   Hook CONFIG files are deliberately out of scope: the four runtimes use incompatible event vocabularies and\n77:   entry shapes, so those files are hand-authored per runtime and cannot be mirror-checked.\n\n(End of file - total 77 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DOCTOR: RUNTIME MIRROR PARITY (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Diagnostic Operator reporting whether every runtime config dir still mirrors its canonical source\npurpose: Detect drift across the agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors that .claude, .codex, .cursor and .devin derive from .opencode\naction: Run the five mirror checkers -> aggregate their verdicts -> report per-surface drift\nskill_owner: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING MODE\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: single-step\n  compliance: MANDATORY\n  execution: read_only\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: single_run\n  validation: read_only_assertion\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml","text":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DOCTOR: RUNTIME MIRROR PARITY (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Diagnostic Operator reporting whether every runtime config dir still mirrors its canonical source\npurpose: Detect drift across the agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors that .claude, .codex, .cursor and .devin derive from .opencode\naction: Run the five mirror checkers -> aggregate their verdicts -> report per-surface drift\nskill_owner: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING MODE\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: single-step\n  compliance: MANDATORY\n  execution: read_only\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: single_run\n  validation: read_only_assertion\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nmutation_boundaries:\n  read_only: true\n  allowed_targets: []\n  forbidden_targets:\n    - \"**/*\"\n  invariant: \"Every checker below is invoked in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT run any generator in write mode, create or delete a symlink, or install a hook config. Repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of a diagnostic.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# UPSTREAM ASSETS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nupstream_assets:\n  runtime_mirrors: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"\n  codex_agents: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/codex/sync-agents.cjs\"\n  codex_prompts: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\"\n  agent_roster: \".opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/agent-roster-mirror-check.cjs\"\n  codex_hooks_installer: \".opencode/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\"\n  pi_agents: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\"\n  pi_prompts: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# INPUTS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ninputs:\n  none: \"This diagnostic takes no arguments. Every checker derives its expected state from the canonical trees and the runtimes' own config files.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# EXECUTION\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nexecution:\n  steps:\n    - \"Run upstream_assets.runtime_mirrors with --check. Covers the cursor/devin agent, command and skill symlink trees plus all four hook discovery mirrors. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n    - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_agents with --check. Covers the generated .codex/agents/*.toml. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n    - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .codex/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n    - \"Run upstream_assets.agent_roster. Covers roster coverage across all five surfaces and rejects a real file where a symlink belongs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift, 2 = canonical dir missing.\"\n    - \"Run upstream_assets.codex_hooks_installer with --check. Covers the user-global ~/.codex/hooks.json against the repo's .codex/hooks.json, including orphaned entries whose .opencode adapter no longer exists on disk. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n    - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_agents with --check. Covers the generated .pi/agents/*.md. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n    - \"Run upstream_assets.pi_prompts with --check. Covers the generated .pi/prompts/*.md stubs. Exit 0 = in sync, 1 = drift.\"\n    - \"Aggregate: report each surface with its own verdict rather than a single pass/fail, so the operator learns which mirror moved.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OUTPUT\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noutput: |\n  STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync.\n  STATUS=DRIFT when any checker reports drift, listing each drifting surface and the repair command for it:\n    runtime mirrors  -> node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n    codex agents     -> node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/codex/sync-agents.cjs\n    codex prompts    -> node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\n    codex hooks      -> node .opencode/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs\n    pi agents        -> node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/pi/sync-agents-pi.cjs\n    pi prompts       -> node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/pi/sync-prompts-pi.cjs\n  The agent roster check has no generator; its drift is repaired by the runtime-mirrors generator or by hand\n  for the authored surfaces (.opencode/agents, .codex/agents).\n  Hook CONFIG files are deliberately out of scope: the four runtimes use incompatible event vocabularies and\n  entry shapes, so those files are hand-authored per runtime and cannot be mirror-checked.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":77,"totalLines":77,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml","time":{"start":1786890752993,"end":1786890752997}},"id":"prt_00afd12f0001bxYBlRqvhB1OLm","sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","messageID":"msg_00afd0060001yDjJ6nAyu3M2YA"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786890753294,"sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_T29hQT3ilYK3fcd9eAyN2077","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update.yaml"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: UPDATE WORKFLOW (CONFIRM - PER-PHASE PROMPT)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Expert Operator running unified spec-kit update in interactive confirm mode\n5: purpose: Execute dependency-safe database rebuild with explicit approval at every phase boundary.\n6: action: flock -> prompt -> probe -> prompt -> migrate -> prompt -> snapshot -> dashboard -> dependency.order -> post.run.validation -> state.log\n7: \n8: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n9: # OPERATING MODE\n10: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n11: operating_mode:\n12:   workflow: sequential_orchestrator\n13:   compliance: MANDATORY\n14:   execution: interactive\n15:   approvals: per_phase_boundary\n16:   tracking: phase_by_phase\n17:   validation: post_run_gold_battery\n18:   state_log: \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.last-run.json\"\n19: \n20: \n21: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n22: # UPDATE ORCHESTRATOR INVARIANT\n23: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n24: update_orchestrator_invariant: |\n25:   The update orchestrator is a single-instance, flock-protected database rebuild\n26:   chain. It executes the dependency DAG in order, snapshots every in-scope DB\n27:   before mutation unless explicitly waived, and restores failed plus downstream\n28:   DBs on retry exhaustion. SIGINT follows ADR-001/ADR-007: set cancel, allow a\n29:   ~5 sec SQLite settle window, restore the in-flight snapshot, log, and exit 130.\n30:   Every abort path — build failure, snapshot failure, dependency failure, SIGINT,\n31:   validation regression — MUST `rm -f .doctor-update.flock` before exit to prevent\n32:   indefinite-lock leak (council Issue 2 sub-finding).\n33: \n34: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n35: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n36: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n37: upstream_assets:\n38:   contract: \"local command design contract\"\n39:   files:\n40:     spec: \"spec.md\"  # orchestrator contract\n41:     decision_record: \"decision-record.md\"  # safety decisions\n42:     council_spec: \"decision-record.md#adr-002\"  # council /doctor:update spec family\n43:     checklist: \"checklist.md#doctor-update-orchestrator\"  # acceptance bars\n44:   pass_policy:\n45:     flock_required: true  # single-instance guard\n46:     full_snapshot_required: true  # full rollback coverage unless --no-snapshot\n47:     retry_backoff_seconds: 5  # bounded retry backoff\n48:     sigint_settle_seconds: 5  # SQLite settle timing before restore\n49:     snapshot_retention_days: 30  # cleanup policy unless --keep-snapshots\n50: \n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: # USER INPUTS\n53: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: user_inputs:\n55:   mode: \"confirm\"\n56:   force: \"[FORCE] boolean\"\n57:   no_snapshot: \"[NO_SNAPSHOT] boolean\"\n58:   cleanup_legacy: \"[CLEANUP_LEGACY] boolean\"\n59:   migrate: \"[MIGRATE] boolean\"\n60:   keep_snapshots: \"[KEEP_SNAPSHOTS] boolean\"\n61:   resume_bootstrap: \"[RESUME_BOOTSTRAP] boolean\"\n62:   skip_status_check: false\n63: \n64: \n65: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n66: # FIELD HANDLING\n67: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n68: field_handling:\n69:   defaults:\n70:     force_empty: \"false\"\n71:     no_snapshot_empty: \"false\"\n72:     cleanup_legacy_empty: \"false\"\n73:     migrate_empty: \"false\"\n74:     keep_snapshots_empty: \"false\"\n75:     resume_bootstrap_empty: \"false\"\n76:   force_policy:\n77:     true: \"warn on active MCP clients and continue\"\n78:     false: \"warn and prompt/abort when active MCP clients are detected\"\n79:   no_snapshot_policy:\n80:     true: \"skip DB snapshots; rollback is unavailable for unsnapshotted DBs\"\n81:     false: \"snapshot every allowed DB before dependency execution\"\n82:   migrate_policy:\n83:     true: \"run migration-manifest Phase 0 before snapshots\"\n84:     false: \"skip migration phase unless version-skip is auto-detected\"\n85:   cleanup_legacy_policy:\n86:     true: \"detect known legacy files from manifest and prompt-delete each\"\n87:     false: \"report legacy findings without deletion prompts\"\n88:   keep_snapshots_policy:\n89:     true: \"skip snapshot cleanup older than 30 days\"\n90:     false: \"cleanup snapshots older than 30 days during final phase\"\n91:   resume_bootstrap_policy:\n92:     true: \"verify .doctor-update.bootstrap.json completed before continuing after a fresh OpenCode restart\"\n93:     false: \"run non-MCP runtime bootstrap and stop with restart_required if bootstrap changed tool-registration inputs\"\n94: \n95: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n96: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n97: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n98: mutation_boundaries:\n99:   allowed_targets:\n100:     - \"mcp-server/database/context-index.sqlite\"  # canonical memory DB\n101:     - \"mcp-server/database/context-index.sqlite.pre-doctor-update.*.bak\"\n102:     - \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database/skill-graph.sqlite\"  # standalone advisor routing graph DB\n103:     - \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database/skill-graph.sqlite.pre-doctor-update.*.bak\"\n104:     - \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/database/deep-loop-graph.sqlite\"  # research/review coverage graph DB\n105:     - \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/database/deep-loop-graph.sqlite.pre-doctor-update.*.bak\"\n106:     - \"mcp-server/database/speckit-eval.db\"  # eval/ablation DB\n107:     - \"mcp-server/database/speckit-eval.db.pre-doctor-update.*.bak\"\n108:     - \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.flock\"  # single-instance lock\n109:     - \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.lock\"\n110:     - \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.last-run.json\"  # orchestrator state log\n111:     - \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.bootstrap.json\"  # pre-MCP bootstrap state\n112:     - \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.bootstrap.lockdir\"  # pre-MCP bootstrap lock\n113:     - \".opencode/skill\"  # compatibility symlink only\n114:     - \".opencode/skill_legacy_backup_*\"  # legacy layout backup before symlink bridge\n115:     - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/dist/**\"  # generated MCP runtime output\n116:     - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/**\"  # generated migration helper output\n117:   forbidden_targets:\n118:     - \"<active-spec-folder>/**/*.md\"  # never write into spec packet docs from /doctor:update\n119:     - \"<active-spec-folder>/description.json\"  # spec metadata belongs to memory-save tooling\n120:     - \"<active-spec-folder>/graph-metadata.json\"  # graph metadata not an orchestrator DB target\n121:     - \".opencode/skills/**/SKILL.md\"  # never edit skill bodies\n122:     - \".opencode/skills/**/graph-metadata.json\"\n123:     - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/**/*.ts\"\n124:     - \".opencode/agents/**/*.md\"\n125:     - \".opencode/commands/doctor/*.md\"\n126:     - \".opencode/commands/doctor/assets/doctor_*.yaml\"\n127:     - \"mcp-server/database/migration-manifest.json\"\n128:     - \"**/migration-manifest.json\"\n129:     - \"direct SQL outside VACUUM INTO snapshot and snapshot restore\"\n130:   validator:\n131:     name: canonical_path_validator\n132:     rule: \"validate allowed_targets and forbidden_targets before snapshot, mutation, rollback, and state-log write\"\n133: \n134: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n135: # STATE LOG SCHEMA\n136: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n137: state_log_schema:\n138:   command: \"/doctor:update\"\n139:   mode: \"confirm\"\n140:   start: \"ISO-8601\"\n141:   end: \"ISO-8601\"\n142:   duration_seconds: \"number\"\n143:   steps:\n144:     - name: \"subsystem\"\n145:       phase: \"number\"\n146:       start: \"ISO-8601\"\n147:       end: \"ISO-8601\"\n148:       exit: \"0|1|130\"\n149:       snapshot_path: \"string|null\"\n150:   final_status: \"ok|failed|rolled_back|cancelled|unrollbackable|restart_required\"\n151: \n152: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n153: # INTERACTIVE PROMPTS\n154: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n155: interactive_prompts:\n156:   phase_boundary_options: [\"approve\", \"inspect details\", \"skip safe optional step\", \"abort\"]\n157:   failure_options: [\"retry from start\", \"rollback snapshot and exit\", \"leave as-is (dangerous)\"]\n158:   regression_options: [\"rollback\", \"accept regression with note\", \"inspect\"]\n159: \n160: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n161: # DEPENDENCY ORDER\n162: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n163: dependency:\n164:   order: [\"context-index\", \"causal-edges-init\", \"skill-graph\", \"advisor\", \"deep-loop-graph\", \"speckit-eval\"]\n165: \n166: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n167: # WORKFLOW\n168: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n169: workflow:\n170:   phase_0_runtime_bootstrap:\n171:     council_line: 0\n172:     approval: \"auto-acknowledge before database flock; this phase uses Bash/Node only, no MCP tools\"\n173:     purpose: \"Resolve the fresh-start paradox: OpenCode can only register MCP tools at process startup, so missing dist/layout must be fixed before MCP-dependent phases run.\"\n174:     launcher_contract:\n175:       mcp_config_entrypoint: \".opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs\"\n176:       invariant: \"MCP configs MUST point to the stable launcher, not directly to mcp-server/dist/context-server.js.\"\n177:       launcher_behavior: \"resolve singular/plural skill layout, build @spec-kit/mcp-server and @spec-kit/scripts when dist is missing, then exec the real MCP server\"\n178:     command_preflight:\n179:       script: \".opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-runtime-bootstrap.sh\"\n180:       command: \"bash .opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-runtime-bootstrap.sh --root . --json\"\n181:       state_log: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.bootstrap.json\"\n182:       no_mcp_tools_allowed: true\n183:     resume_rule:\n184:       if_resume_bootstrap_true: \"require bootstrap state status=complete and generated artifacts present; continue to phase_1_flock_acquire\"\n185:       if_resume_bootstrap_false_and_restart_required_true: \"write .doctor-update.last-run.json with final_status=restart_required, release any bootstrap lock, stop before database flock\"\n186:       restart_message: \"BOOTSTRAP_COMPLETE_RESTART_REQUIRED: restart OpenCode so MCP tools register, then rerun /doctor:update --resume-bootstrap\"\n187:       max_reentry_count: 1\n188:     required_artifacts:\n189:       - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/dist/context-server.js\"\n190:       - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js\"\n191:       - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/spec-folder/generate-description.js\"\n192:     failure:\n193:       emit_error: \"runtime bootstrap failed before MCP registration; inspect .doctor-update.bootstrap.json\"\n194:       final_status: \"failed\"\n195:       exit_code: 1\n196: \n197:   phase_1_flock_acquire:\n198:     council_line: 1\n199:     approval: \"prompt before acquiring lock\"\n200:     flock: \"ACQUIRE flock at mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.flock; refuse if held\"\n201:     pid_file: \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.lock\"\n202:     stale_lock_rule: \"refuse if PID-file stale-locked >2h\"\n203:     refusal_message: \"holding PID + start timestamp\"\n204: \n205:   phase_1_5_mcp_server_bootability:\n206:     council_line: 1\n207:     approval: \"auto-acknowledge in confirm workflow (short tier per markdown)\"\n208:     preflight_check: |\n209:       stat .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/dist/context-server.js\n210:     rationale: \"Defense-in-depth after Phase 0 and the MCP launcher. MCP tools listed in /doctor:update allowed-tools cannot be invoked unless the MCP server is built and bootable.\"\n211:     if_dist_missing:\n212:       action: \"run the maintained non-MCP bootstrap script, then stop for fresh OpenCode startup instead of continuing into MCP phases\"\n213:       commands: |\n214:         bash .opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-runtime-bootstrap.sh --root .\n215:       timeout_seconds: 240\n216:       on_build_failure:\n217:         emit_error: \"system-spec-kit runtime build failed; cannot proceed with database operations\"\n218:         release_flock: \"rm -f .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.flock .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.lock\"\n219:         exit_code: 1\n220:       on_build_success:\n221:         final_status: \"restart_required\"\n222:         emit_message: \"BOOTSTRAP_COMPLETE_RESTART_REQUIRED: restart OpenCode so MCP tools register, then rerun /doctor:update --resume-bootstrap\"\n223:     if_dist_present:\n224:       action: \"verify timestamp newer than 30 days OR mcp-server/lib/**/*.ts (catch stale builds)\"\n225:       stale_threshold_days: 30\n226:       on_stale: \"warn but proceed; recommend rebuild outside flock\"\n227:     flock_release_invariant: \"On ANY abort path from this phase forward (failure, SIGINT, exception), release the flock file BEFORE exit. Each downstream phase inherits this invariant.\"\n228: \n229:   phase_2_probe_mcp_activity:\n230:     council_line: 2\n231:     approval: \"prompt before probing active clients\"\n232:     probe: \"PROBE other MCP-client activity\"\n233:     active_behavior: \"if active, warn and prompt; --force marks force-ok\"\n234: \n235:   phase_8_migration_phase_0:\n236:     council_line: 8\n237:     approval: \"prompt before migration manifest Phase 0\"\n238:     condition: |\n239:       user_inputs.migrate == true\n240:       OR (\n241:         file_system_signals_detected >= 2 of [\n242:           (.opencode/skill exists AND is a directory NOT a symlink),\n243:           (.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/dist/context-server.js does NOT exist),\n244:           (find . -path './.opencode' -prune -o -name 'memory' -type d -print | grep -q .),\n245:           (find specs -mindepth 2 -name 'spec.md' | first-match dirname has no description.json)\n246:         ]\n247:       )\n248:       ELSE refuse to proceed when version detection ambiguous and neither --migrate nor --no-migrate flag was passed.\n249:     file_system_signals:\n250:       signal_a:\n251:         check: \"[ -d .opencode/skill ] && [ ! -L .opencode/skill ]\"\n252:         meaning: \"v3.3-era singular directory present as a real directory (not bridge symlink)\"\n253:       signal_b:\n254:         check: \"[ ! -f .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/dist/context-server.js ]\"\n255:         meaning: \"MCP server dist missing — fresh tarball install or post-clone state\"\n256:       signal_c:\n257:         check: \"find specs -name 'memory' -type d -print -quit 2>/dev/null | grep -q .\"\n258:         meaning: \"legacy memory/ folders inside any spec packet (v3.3 continuity surface)\"\n259:       signal_d:\n260:         check: |\n261:           if [ -d .opencode/specs ]; then\n262:             # FIX-12: removed `head -1` (was limiting check to FIRST folder only).\n263:             # Now iterates ALL spec.md until grep -q hits the first \"missing\" emission and short-circuits.\n264:             find specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 5 -name 'spec.md' 2>/dev/null \\\n265:               | while IFS= read -r f; do\n266:                 dir=$(dirname \"$f\")\n267:                 [ ! -f \"$dir/description.json\" ] && echo missing\n268:               done | grep -q missing\n269:           else\n270:             false\n271:           fi\n272:         meaning: \"spec folders exist but lack description.json (v3.4-required metadata not backfilled from v3.3)\"\n273:     auto_migrate_threshold: 2\n274:     rationale: \"package.json version field is a build-time placeholder ('0.0.0' in release tarballs), so version detection MUST use file-system signals instead. Council FIX-03.\"\n275:     migration: \"run migration-manifest.json Phase 0 before snapshots\"\n276:     gap_detected: \"refuse to proceed if manifest gap detected\"\n277:     directory_layout_bridge:\n278:       precondition: \"both .opencode/skill/ and .opencode/skills/ directories exist (legacy v3.3 layout + current v3.4 layout)\"\n279:       detect_command: |\n280:         [ -d .opencode/skill ] && [ -d .opencode/skills ] && [ ! -L .opencode/skill ]\n281:       bridge_action: |\n282:         rm -rf .opencode/skill_legacy_backup_$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ) 2>/dev/null\n283:         mv .opencode/skill .opencode/skill_legacy_backup_$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)\n284:         ln -sf skills .opencode/skill\n285:       on_symlink_failure:\n286:         action: \"write per-file remediation instructions\"\n287:         instruction_file: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.config-instructions\"\n288:         content_template: |\n289:           # /doctor:update remediation: directory rename\n290:           # Run these commands manually to update v3.3 -> v3.4 paths:\n291:           sed -i.bak 's|\\.opencode/skill/|.opencode/skills/|g' .mcp.json opencode.json 2>/dev/null\n292:           # Then manually verify .mcp.json and opencode.json are correct.\n293:       idempotency: \"if .opencode/skill is already a symlink to skills, skip\"\n294:     spec_metadata_backfill:\n295:       precondition: \"signal_d positive (spec folders exist but lack description.json) OR signal_c positive (legacy memory/ folders detected)\"\n296:       rationale: \"v3.3 spec packets lack the description.json + graph-metadata.json files that v3.4 requires for memory_index_scan visibility. Without backfill, Phase 5.2 silently skips all v3.3 packets — see Issue 11 in council Round 2 backlog.\"\n297:       mutation_boundary_exception: \"Phase 8 INVOKES the sanctioned backfill scripts (generate-description.js + backfill-graph-metadata.js). The orchestrator does not edit description.json/graph-metadata.json directly; it delegates to maintained tooling per migration-manifest M-3.3.0.0-002 fallback_operation.\"\n298:       step_a_graph_metadata_backfill:\n299:         command: |\n300:           # FIX-13: --active-only skips z_archive/z-future paths that the script's path-validator\n301:           # rejects with \"Spec folder is not under a supported specs root\" — those archive trees\n302:           # are outside graph-metadata backfill's traversal contract. Note: this is separate from\n303:           # the memory index scope. Per the archive-retention fix (commit b062b12b4), z_archive content IS\n304:           # indexed into the memory DB and deprioritized via ARCHIVE_MULTIPLIERS 0.1; only\n305:           # graph-metadata backfill's path-validator skips it.\n306:           node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js --active-only 2>&1 \\\n307:             | tee .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.backfill-graph.log\n308:         timeout_seconds: 300\n309:         on_failure: \"warn but proceed (Phase 5.2 indexing will be partial); record failure in state log\"\n310:       step_b_description_backfill:\n311:         command: |\n312:           # Loop over spec folders missing description.json\n313:           missing_count=0\n314:           created_count=0\n315:           failed_count=0\n316:           while read -r spec_md; do\n317:             dir=$(dirname \"$spec_md\")\n318:             if [ ! -f \"$dir/description.json\" ]; then\n319:               missing_count=$((missing_count + 1))\n320:               if node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/spec-folder/generate-description.js \\\n321:                 \"$dir\" \"$(pwd)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n322:                 created_count=$((created_count + 1))\n323:               else\n324:                 failed_count=$((failed_count + 1))\n325:               fi\n326:             fi\n327:           done < <(find specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 5 -name 'spec.md' 2>/dev/null)\n328:           echo \"{\\\"missing\\\":$missing_count,\\\"created\\\":$created_count,\\\"failed\\\":$failed_count}\" \\\n329:             > .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.backfill-description.log\n330:         timeout_seconds: 600\n331:         on_failure: \"warn per-folder; aggregate failed_count for state log\"\n332:       report_to_dashboard: \"Phase 4 dashboard adds row 'spec-metadata-backfill: created=N, failed=M' when this sub-action runs\"\n333:     legacy_memory_md_detection:\n334:       precondition: \"always run when Phase 8 is triggered\"\n335:       rationale: \"v3.3 used memory/*.md files inside spec folders for continuity. v3.4 moved continuity to _memory.continuity frontmatter blocks in implementation-summary.md. The migration is NOT fully automatable — content review required per migration-manifest M-3.3.0.0-001 fallback_operation. Phase 8 detects + reports, the user runs /memory:save manually after review.\"\n336:       detection: |\n337:         find specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 6 -path '*/memory/*.md' \\\n338:           -not -path '*/scratch/*' -not -path '*/z_archive/*' 2>/dev/null \\\n339:           | tee .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.legacy-memory-files.log \\\n340:           | wc -l\n341:       action_on_findings:\n342:         do_not_auto_migrate: \"respecting manifest M-3.3.0.0-001 'review first' policy\"\n343:         write_summary_log: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.legacy-memory-files.log\"\n344:         recommend_to_user: |\n345:           # Emit at end of Phase 8:\n346:           if [ \"$LEGACY_MEMORY_COUNT\" -gt 0 ]; then\n347:             echo \"\"\n348:             echo \"/doctor:update detected $LEGACY_MEMORY_COUNT legacy memory/*.md files in spec packets.\"\n349:             echo \"These are v3.3 continuity artifacts that were superseded by _memory.continuity frontmatter in v3.4.\"\n350:             echo \"\"\n351:             echo \"RECOMMENDED MANUAL STEP: review the files listed in .doctor-update.legacy-memory-files.log,\"\n352:             echo \"then run \\`/memory:save\\` for each affected packet to migrate continuity into the v3.4 frontmatter format.\"\n353:             echo \"\"\n354:           fi\n355: \n356:   phase_3_snapshot_all_databases:\n357:     council_line: 3\n358:     approval: \"prompt before snapshot; include disk use estimate\"\n359:     condition: \"unless --no-snapshot\"\n360:     snapshot: \"SNAPSHOT every *.sqlite via VACUUM INTO\"\n361:     filename: \"<name>.pre-doctor-update.<version>.<timestamp>.bak\"\n362:     disk_free: \"refuse if disk free < 2x DB total\"\n363:     post_snapshot_hook: |\n364:       # Preserve original mtime on snapshot copies so age-based recovery decisions stay accurate.\n365:       # VACUUM INTO creates a new file with current mtime by default; reset to source mtime.\n366:       for src in mcp-server/database/*.sqlite mcp-server/database/*.db; do\n367:         [ -f \"$src\" ] || continue\n368:         for bak in \"$src\".pre-doctor-update.*.bak; do\n369:           [ -f \"$bak\" ] || continue\n370:           touch -r \"$src\" \"$bak\"\n371:         done\n372:       done\n373:     rationale: \"VACUUM INTO sets mtime to the snapshot moment, not the source's last-modified time. For age-based recovery decisions, snapshot mtime should reflect the source state being checkpointed. Council FIX-05.\"\n374: \n375:   phase_4_status_dashboard:\n376:     council_line: 4\n377:     approval: \"prompt after rendering dashboard and before selecting actions\"\n378:     cross_subsystem_dashboard:\n379:       rows: [\"context-index\", \"causal-edges\", \"skill-graph\", \"advisor\", \"deep-loop\", \"eval\"]\n380:       columns: [\"status\", \"age\", \"coverage\", \"recommended action\"]\n381:       coverage_column_rationale: \"context-index row populated by FIX-10 post_run_count_skipped output; other rows show n/a unless their tool surfaces a coverage metric\"\n382: \n383:   phase_5_dependency_order_execute:\n384:     council_line: 4\n385:     approval: \"prompt before each dependency step\"\n386:     dependency.order: [\"context-index\", \"causal-edges-init\", \"skill-graph\", \"advisor\", \"deep-loop-graph\", \"speckit-eval\"]\n387:     test_failure_injection:\n388:       env_var: \"SPECKIT_FAIL_STEP\"\n389:       scope: \"disposable workspace tests only\"\n390:       rule: \"Before executing each dependency step, if SPECKIT_FAIL_STEP exactly equals the dependency step name, inject a synthetic failure after snapshots and before mutating that step.\"\n391:       example: \"SPECKIT_FAIL_STEP=causal-edges-init\"\n392:       state_log_requirement: \"Record injected_failure=true, failed_step=<step>, and final_status=rolled_back when rollback is selected.\"\n393:     execute:\n394:       context-index:\n395:         action: \"memory_index_scan({ incremental: false, force: true })\"\n396:         post_run_count_skipped: |\n397:           # Coverage gap = on-disk spec folders (those containing spec.md) the index\n398:           # does not cover, computed as a set-difference (NOT total-minus-indexed: the\n399:           # index holds historical/phase folders, so a raw subtraction is meaningless).\n400:           # memory_index stores spec_folder relative to .opencode/specs and some legacy\n401:           # rows keep the prefix, so both sides are prefix-normalized before comparison;\n402:           # ln/ + external/ are excluded to mirror the memory index-scope policy. The\n403:           # canonical DB is resolved via shared/embeddings/profile.js (post vector-shard\n404:           # split it is the single context-index.sqlite; only vector shards are\n405:           # per-profile). The node read is cwd-independent and read-only so it never\n406:           # contends with the daemon's single-writer lock.\n407:           coverage=$(find specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 5 -name 'spec.md' 2>/dev/null \\\n408:             | sed 's#/spec.md$##' \\\n409:             | node -e \"\n410:                 const fs = require('fs'), path = require('path');\n411:                 const dir = '.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database';\n412:                 const LOG = path.join(dir, '.doctor-update.context-index-coverage.log');\n413:                 let Database; try { Database = require(path.resolve(dir, '../node_modules/better-sqlite3')); } catch (e) { Database = require('better-sqlite3'); }\n414:                 const norm = (s) => String(s).replace(/^[.][/]/, '').replace(/^[.]opencode[/]specs[/]/, '').replace(/^specs[/]/, '').replace(/[/]+\\$/, '');\n415:                 const excluded = (p) => /(^|[/])(ln|external)([/]|\\$)/.test(p);\n416:                 const onDisk = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8').split('\\n').map(norm).filter((s) => s && !excluded(s));\n417:                 (async () => {\n418:                   let dbPath;\n419:                   try { const m = await import(path.resolve(dir, '../../shared/dist/embeddings/profile.js')); dbPath = m.resolveActiveProfileDbPath(undefined, dir); }\n420:                   catch (e) { dbPath = path.join(dir, 'context-index.sqlite'); }\n421:                   let indexed = new Set();\n422:                   if (fs.existsSync(dbPath)) {\n423:                     const db = new Database(dbPath, { readonly: true, fileMustExist: true });\n424:                     indexed = new Set(db.prepare('SELECT DISTINCT spec_folder FROM memory_index WHERE spec_folder IS NOT NULL').all().map((r) => norm(r.spec_folder)));\n425:                     db.close();\n426:                   }\n427:                   const missing = onDisk.filter((f) => !indexed.has(f));\n428:                   fs.writeFileSync(LOG, JSON.stringify({ total_specs: onDisk.length, indexed: onDisk.length - missing.length, skipped: missing.length, db: path.basename(dbPath), missing: missing.slice(0, 50) }));\n429:                   process.stdout.write(onDisk.length + ' ' + (onDisk.length - missing.length) + ' ' + missing.length);\n430:                 })().catch((e) => { try { fs.writeFileSync(LOG, JSON.stringify({ error: String((e && e.message) || e) })); } catch (_) {} process.stdout.write('0 0 0'); });\n431:               \" 2>/dev/null || echo \"0 0 0\")\n432:           total_specs=$(printf '%s' \"$coverage\" | cut -d' ' -f1)\n433:           indexed_specs=$(printf '%s' \"$coverage\" | cut -d' ' -f2)\n434:           skipped=$(printf '%s' \"$coverage\" | cut -d' ' -f3)\n435:         report_when_skipped: |\n436:           # Self-contained: reads the coverage log written by post_run_count_skipped,\n437:           # so it does not depend on shell vars surviving between steps.\n438:           LOG=.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.context-index-coverage.log\n439:           skipped=$(node -e \"try { console.log(JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync(process.argv[1], 'utf8')).skipped || 0); } catch (e) { console.log(0); }\" \"$LOG\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\n440:           if [ \"${skipped:-0}\" -gt 0 ]; then\n441:             node -e \"\n442:               const d = JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync(process.argv[1], 'utf8'));\n443:               console.log('WARNING: context-index coverage gap detected');\n444:               console.log('  total spec folders found: ' + d.total_specs);\n445:               console.log('  indexed:                  ' + d.indexed);\n446:               console.log('  skipped:                  ' + d.skipped + ' (exist on disk but absent from the index)');\n447:               if (Array.isArray(d.missing) && d.missing.length) console.log('  e.g.: ' + d.missing.slice(0, 5).join(', ') + (d.skipped > 5 ? ' ...' : ''));\n448:               console.log('  run Phase 8 backfill OR /memory:save per affected packet to fix (or add the path to the index-scope exclusions if intentional)');\n449:             \" \"$LOG\"\n450:           fi\n451:       causal-edges-init: \"memory_causal_link(...) for high-confidence missing lineage\"\n452:       skill-graph: \"mk_skill_advisor.skill_graph_scan({})\"\n453:       advisor: \"mk_skill_advisor.advisor_rebuild({ force: true }) + mk_skill_advisor.advisor_validate({})\"\n454:       deep-loop-graph: \"deep_loop_graph_upsert(...)\"\n455:       speckit-eval: \"eval_run_ablation({})\"\n456:     failure:\n457:       council_line: 5\n458:       retry: \"one retry with 5-sec backoff\"\n459:       after_retry_failure: \"prompt retry / rollback / leave\"\n460: \n461:   phase_5_5_post_dependency_checkpoint:\n462:     council_line: 5\n463:     approval: \"auto-acknowledge unless --keep-snapshots is set\"\n464:     optional: true\n465:     detect_command: |\n466:       comm -13 \\\n467:         <(ls mcp-server/database/*.pre-doctor-update.*.bak 2>/dev/null | sed 's/\\.pre-doctor-update\\..*\\.bak$//' | sort -u) \\\n468:         <(ls mcp-server/database/*.sqlite mcp-server/database/*.db 2>/dev/null | sort -u)\n469:     checkpoint_action: |\n470:       # For each newly-created DB, take a \"post-bootstrap\" checkpoint snapshot.\n471:       for new_db in $(comm -13 ...); do\n472:         sqlite3 \"$new_db\" \".backup '${new_db}.post-doctor-update.${VERSION}.${TIMESTAMP}.bak'\" 2>/dev/null \\\n473:           || cp -p \"$new_db\" \"${new_db}.post-doctor-update.${VERSION}.${TIMESTAMP}.bak\"\n474:       done\n475:     rationale: \"Phase 3 snapshots only EXISTING DBs. On fresh install, all DBs are created during Phase 5, leaving no rollback target if Phase 7 validation fails. Phase 5.5 fills this gap. Council FIX-06.\"\n476: \n477:   phase_6_sigint_cancel_contract:\n478:     council_line: 6\n479:     SIGINT: \"set cancel flag; let current SQLite tx commit/abort; restore snapshot of in-flight DB; log cancelled by user; exit 130\"\n480:     settle_window: \"~5 sec per ADR-001\"\n481: \n482:   phase_7_post_run_validation:\n483:     council_line: 7\n484:     approval: \"prompt before accepting validation results when any warning exists\"\n485:     post.run.validation:\n486:       - \"existence + schema-version + row-count delta within bounds\"\n487:       - \"gold-battery sanity check per DB\"\n488:     regression: \"prompt\"\n489: \n490:   phase_9_legacy_cleanup:\n491:     council_line: 9\n492:     condition: \"user_inputs.cleanup_legacy == true\"\n493:     legacy: \"detect known-legacy files per migration-manifest\"\n494:     deletion: \"prompt-delete each; never silent\"\n495: \n496:   phase_10_state_log_unlock_cleanup:\n497:     council_line: 10\n498:     state.log: \"write .doctor-update.last-run.json with timestamps, durations, snapshot paths\"\n499:     release_flock: true\n500:     cleanup: \"prompt before deleting snapshots >30 days unless --keep-snapshots\"\n501: \n502: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n503: # OUTPUT FORMAT\n504: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n505: output_format: |\n506:   Render phase decisions, cross-subsystem health dashboard, validation results, state log path, and STATUS.\n\n(End of file - total 506 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DOCTOR: UPDATE WORKFLOW (CONFIRM - PER-PHASE PROMPT)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Expert Operator running unified spec-kit update in interactive confirm mode\npurpose: Execute dependency-safe database rebuild with explicit approval at every phase boundary.\naction: flock -> prompt -> probe -> prompt -> migrate -> prompt -> snapshot -> dashboard -> dependency.order -> post.run.validation -> state.log\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING MODE\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: sequential_orchestrator\n  compliance: MANDATORY\n  execution: interactive\n  approvals: per_phase_boundary\n  tracking: phase_by_phase\n  validation: post_run_gold_battery\n  state_log: \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.last-run.json\"\n\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update.yaml","text":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DOCTOR: UPDATE WORKFLOW (CONFIRM - PER-PHASE PROMPT)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Expert Operator running unified spec-kit update in interactive confirm mode\npurpose: Execute dependency-safe database rebuild with explicit approval at every phase boundary.\naction: flock -> prompt -> probe -> prompt -> migrate -> prompt -> snapshot -> dashboard -> dependency.order -> post.run.validation -> state.log\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING MODE\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: sequential_orchestrator\n  compliance: MANDATORY\n  execution: interactive\n  approvals: per_phase_boundary\n  tracking: phase_by_phase\n  validation: post_run_gold_battery\n  state_log: \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.last-run.json\"\n\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# UPDATE ORCHESTRATOR INVARIANT\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nupdate_orchestrator_invariant: |\n  The update orchestrator is a single-instance, flock-protected database rebuild\n  chain. It executes the dependency DAG in order, snapshots every in-scope DB\n  before mutation unless explicitly waived, and restores failed plus downstream\n  DBs on retry exhaustion. SIGINT follows ADR-001/ADR-007: set cancel, allow a\n  ~5 sec SQLite settle window, restore the in-flight snapshot, log, and exit 130.\n  Every abort path — build failure, snapshot failure, dependency failure, SIGINT,\n  validation regression — MUST `rm -f .doctor-update.flock` before exit to prevent\n  indefinite-lock leak (council Issue 2 sub-finding).\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# UPSTREAM ASSETS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nupstream_assets:\n  contract: \"local command design contract\"\n  files:\n    spec: \"spec.md\"  # orchestrator contract\n    decision_record: \"decision-record.md\"  # safety decisions\n    council_spec: \"decision-record.md#adr-002\"  # council /doctor:update spec family\n    checklist: \"checklist.md#doctor-update-orchestrator\"  # acceptance bars\n  pass_policy:\n    flock_required: true  # single-instance guard\n    full_snapshot_required: true  # full rollback coverage unless --no-snapshot\n    retry_backoff_seconds: 5  # bounded retry backoff\n    sigint_settle_seconds: 5  # SQLite settle timing before restore\n    snapshot_retention_days: 30  # cleanup policy unless --keep-snapshots\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# USER INPUTS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nuser_inputs:\n  mode: \"confirm\"\n  force: \"[FORCE] boolean\"\n  no_snapshot: \"[NO_SNAPSHOT] boolean\"\n  cleanup_legacy: \"[CLEANUP_LEGACY] boolean\"\n  migrate: \"[MIGRATE] boolean\"\n  keep_snapshots: \"[KEEP_SNAPSHOTS] boolean\"\n  resume_bootstrap: \"[RESUME_BOOTSTRAP] boolean\"\n  skip_status_check: false\n\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# FIELD HANDLING\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nfield_handling:\n  defaults:\n    force_empty: \"false\"\n    no_snapshot_empty: \"false\"\n    cleanup_legacy_empty: \"false\"\n    migrate_empty: \"false\"\n    keep_snapshots_empty: \"false\"\n    resume_bootstrap_empty: \"false\"\n  force_policy:\n    true: \"warn on active MCP clients and continue\"\n    false: \"warn and prompt/abort when active MCP clients are detected\"\n  no_snapshot_policy:\n    true: \"skip DB snapshots; rollback is unavailable for unsnapshotted DBs\"\n    false: \"snapshot every allowed DB before dependency execution\"\n  migrate_policy:\n    true: \"run migration-manifest Phase 0 before snapshots\"\n    false: \"skip migration phase unless version-skip is auto-detected\"\n  cleanup_legacy_policy:\n    true: \"detect known legacy files from manifest and prompt-delete each\"\n    false: \"report legacy findings without deletion prompts\"\n  keep_snapshots_policy:\n    true: \"skip snapshot cleanup older than 30 days\"\n    false: \"cleanup snapshots older than 30 days during final phase\"\n  resume_bootstrap_policy:\n    true: \"verify .doctor-update.bootstrap.json completed before continuing after a fresh OpenCode restart\"\n    false: \"run non-MCP runtime bootstrap and stop with restart_required if bootstrap changed tool-registration inputs\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nmutation_boundaries:\n  allowed_targets:\n    - \"mcp-server/database/context-index.sqlite\"  # canonical memory DB\n    - \"mcp-server/database/context-index.sqlite.pre-doctor-update.*.bak\"\n    - \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database/skill-graph.sqlite\"  # standalone advisor routing graph DB\n    - \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database/skill-graph.sqlite.pre-doctor-update.*.bak\"\n    - \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/database/deep-loop-graph.sqlite\"  # research/review coverage graph DB\n    - \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/database/deep-loop-graph.sqlite.pre-doctor-update.*.bak\"\n    - \"mcp-server/database/speckit-eval.db\"  # eval/ablation DB\n    - \"mcp-server/database/speckit-eval.db.pre-doctor-update.*.bak\"\n    - \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.flock\"  # single-instance lock\n    - \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.lock\"\n    - \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.last-run.json\"  # orchestrator state log\n    - \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.bootstrap.json\"  # pre-MCP bootstrap state\n    - \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.bootstrap.lockdir\"  # pre-MCP bootstrap lock\n    - \".opencode/skill\"  # compatibility symlink only\n    - \".opencode/skill_legacy_backup_*\"  # legacy layout backup before symlink bridge\n    - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/dist/**\"  # generated MCP runtime output\n    - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/**\"  # generated migration helper output\n  forbidden_targets:\n    - \"<active-spec-folder>/**/*.md\"  # never write into spec packet docs from /doctor:update\n    - \"<active-spec-folder>/description.json\"  # spec metadata belongs to memory-save tooling\n    - \"<active-spec-folder>/graph-metadata.json\"  # graph metadata not an orchestrator DB target\n    - \".opencode/skills/**/SKILL.md\"  # never edit skill bodies\n    - \".opencode/skills/**/graph-metadata.json\"\n    - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/**/*.ts\"\n    - \".opencode/agents/**/*.md\"\n    - \".opencode/commands/doctor/*.md\"\n    - \".opencode/commands/doctor/assets/doctor_*.yaml\"\n    - \"mcp-server/database/migration-manifest.json\"\n    - \"**/migration-manifest.json\"\n    - \"direct SQL outside VACUUM INTO snapshot and snapshot restore\"\n  validator:\n    name: canonical_path_validator\n    rule: \"validate allowed_targets and forbidden_targets before snapshot, mutation, rollback, and state-log write\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# STATE LOG SCHEMA\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nstate_log_schema:\n  command: \"/doctor:update\"\n  mode: \"confirm\"\n  start: \"ISO-8601\"\n  end: \"ISO-8601\"\n  duration_seconds: \"number\"\n  steps:\n    - name: \"subsystem\"\n      phase: \"number\"\n      start: \"ISO-8601\"\n      end: \"ISO-8601\"\n      exit: \"0|1|130\"\n      snapshot_path: \"string|null\"\n  final_status: \"ok|failed|rolled_back|cancelled|unrollbackable|restart_required\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# INTERACTIVE PROMPTS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ninteractive_prompts:\n  phase_boundary_options: [\"approve\", \"inspect details\", \"skip safe optional step\", \"abort\"]\n  failure_options: [\"retry from start\", \"rollback snapshot and exit\", \"leave as-is (dangerous)\"]\n  regression_options: [\"rollback\", \"accept regression with note\", \"inspect\"]\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEPENDENCY ORDER\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ndependency:\n  order: [\"context-index\", \"causal-edges-init\", \"skill-graph\", \"advisor\", \"deep-loop-graph\", \"speckit-eval\"]\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# WORKFLOW\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nworkflow:\n  phase_0_runtime_bootstrap:\n    council_line: 0\n    approval: \"auto-acknowledge before database flock; this phase uses Bash/Node only, no MCP tools\"\n    purpose: \"Resolve the fresh-start paradox: OpenCode can only register MCP tools at process startup, so missing dist/layout must be fixed before MCP-dependent phases run.\"\n    launcher_contract:\n      mcp_config_entrypoint: \".opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs\"\n      invariant: \"MCP configs MUST point to the stable launcher, not directly to mcp-server/dist/context-server.js.\"\n      launcher_behavior: \"resolve singular/plural skill layout, build @spec-kit/mcp-server and @spec-kit/scripts when dist is missing, then exec the real MCP server\"\n    command_preflight:\n      script: \".opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-runtime-bootstrap.sh\"\n      command: \"bash .opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-runtime-bootstrap.sh --root . --json\"\n      state_log: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.bootstrap.json\"\n      no_mcp_tools_allowed: true\n    resume_rule:\n      if_resume_bootstrap_true: \"require bootstrap state status=complete and generated artifacts present; continue to phase_1_flock_acquire\"\n      if_resume_bootstrap_false_and_restart_required_true: \"write .doctor-update.last-run.json with final_status=restart_required, release any bootstrap lock, stop before database flock\"\n      restart_message: \"BOOTSTRAP_COMPLETE_RESTART_REQUIRED: restart OpenCode so MCP tools register, then rerun /doctor:update --resume-bootstrap\"\n      max_reentry_count: 1\n    required_artifacts:\n      - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/dist/context-server.js\"\n      - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js\"\n      - \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/spec-folder/generate-description.js\"\n    failure:\n      emit_error: \"runtime bootstrap failed before MCP registration; inspect .doctor-update.bootstrap.json\"\n      final_status: \"failed\"\n      exit_code: 1\n\n  phase_1_flock_acquire:\n    council_line: 1\n    approval: \"prompt before acquiring lock\"\n    flock: \"ACQUIRE flock at mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.flock; refuse if held\"\n    pid_file: \"mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.lock\"\n    stale_lock_rule: \"refuse if PID-file stale-locked >2h\"\n    refusal_message: \"holding PID + start timestamp\"\n\n  phase_1_5_mcp_server_bootability:\n    council_line: 1\n    approval: \"auto-acknowledge in confirm workflow (short tier per markdown)\"\n    preflight_check: |\n      stat .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/dist/context-server.js\n    rationale: \"Defense-in-depth after Phase 0 and the MCP launcher. MCP tools listed in /doctor:update allowed-tools cannot be invoked unless the MCP server is built and bootable.\"\n    if_dist_missing:\n      action: \"run the maintained non-MCP bootstrap script, then stop for fresh OpenCode startup instead of continuing into MCP phases\"\n      commands: |\n        bash .opencode/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-runtime-bootstrap.sh --root .\n      timeout_seconds: 240\n      on_build_failure:\n        emit_error: \"system-spec-kit runtime build failed; cannot proceed with database operations\"\n        release_flock: \"rm -f .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.flock .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.lock\"\n        exit_code: 1\n      on_build_success:\n        final_status: \"restart_required\"\n        emit_message: \"BOOTSTRAP_COMPLETE_RESTART_REQUIRED: restart OpenCode so MCP tools register, then rerun /doctor:update --resume-bootstrap\"\n    if_dist_present:\n      action: \"verify timestamp newer than 30 days OR mcp-server/lib/**/*.ts (catch stale builds)\"\n      stale_threshold_days: 30\n      on_stale: \"warn but proceed; recommend rebuild outside flock\"\n    flock_release_invariant: \"On ANY abort path from this phase forward (failure, SIGINT, exception), release the flock file BEFORE exit. Each downstream phase inherits this invariant.\"\n\n  phase_2_probe_mcp_activity:\n    council_line: 2\n    approval: \"prompt before probing active clients\"\n    probe: \"PROBE other MCP-client activity\"\n    active_behavior: \"if active, warn and prompt; --force marks force-ok\"\n\n  phase_8_migration_phase_0:\n    council_line: 8\n    approval: \"prompt before migration manifest Phase 0\"\n    condition: |\n      user_inputs.migrate == true\n      OR (\n        file_system_signals_detected >= 2 of [\n          (.opencode/skill exists AND is a directory NOT a symlink),\n          (.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/dist/context-server.js does NOT exist),\n          (find . -path './.opencode' -prune -o -name 'memory' -type d -print | grep -q .),\n          (find specs -mindepth 2 -name 'spec.md' | first-match dirname has no description.json)\n        ]\n      )\n      ELSE refuse to proceed when version detection ambiguous and neither --migrate nor --no-migrate flag was passed.\n    file_system_signals:\n      signal_a:\n        check: \"[ -d .opencode/skill ] && [ ! -L .opencode/skill ]\"\n        meaning: \"v3.3-era singular directory present as a real directory (not bridge symlink)\"\n      signal_b:\n        check: \"[ ! -f .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/dist/context-server.js ]\"\n        meaning: \"MCP server dist missing — fresh tarball install or post-clone state\"\n      signal_c:\n        check: \"find specs -name 'memory' -type d -print -quit 2>/dev/null | grep -q .\"\n        meaning: \"legacy memory/ folders inside any spec packet (v3.3 continuity surface)\"\n      signal_d:\n        check: |\n          if [ -d .opencode/specs ]; then\n            # FIX-12: removed `head -1` (was limiting check to FIRST folder only).\n            # Now iterates ALL spec.md until grep -q hits the first \"missing\" emission and short-circuits.\n            find specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 5 -name 'spec.md' 2>/dev/null \\\n              | while IFS= read -r f; do\n                dir=$(dirname \"$f\")\n                [ ! -f \"$dir/description.json\" ] && echo missing\n              done | grep -q missing\n          else\n            false\n          fi\n        meaning: \"spec folders exist but lack description.json (v3.4-required metadata not backfilled from v3.3)\"\n    auto_migrate_threshold: 2\n    rationale: \"package.json version field is a build-time placeholder ('0.0.0' in release tarballs), so version detection MUST use file-system signals instead. Council FIX-03.\"\n    migration: \"run migration-manifest.json Phase 0 before snapshots\"\n    gap_detected: \"refuse to proceed if manifest gap detected\"\n    directory_layout_bridge:\n      precondition: \"both .opencode/skill/ and .opencode/skills/ directories exist (legacy v3.3 layout + current v3.4 layout)\"\n      detect_command: |\n        [ -d .opencode/skill ] && [ -d .opencode/skills ] && [ ! -L .opencode/skill ]\n      bridge_action: |\n        rm -rf .opencode/skill_legacy_backup_$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ) 2>/dev/null\n        mv .opencode/skill .opencode/skill_legacy_backup_$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)\n        ln -sf skills .opencode/skill\n      on_symlink_failure:\n        action: \"write per-file remediation instructions\"\n        instruction_file: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.config-instructions\"\n        content_template: |\n          # /doctor:update remediation: directory rename\n          # Run these commands manually to update v3.3 -> v3.4 paths:\n          sed -i.bak 's|\\.opencode/skill/|.opencode/skills/|g' .mcp.json opencode.json 2>/dev/null\n          # Then manually verify .mcp.json and opencode.json are correct.\n      idempotency: \"if .opencode/skill is already a symlink to skills, skip\"\n    spec_metadata_backfill:\n      precondition: \"signal_d positive (spec folders exist but lack description.json) OR signal_c positive (legacy memory/ folders detected)\"\n      rationale: \"v3.3 spec packets lack the description.json + graph-metadata.json files that v3.4 requires for memory_index_scan visibility. Without backfill, Phase 5.2 silently skips all v3.3 packets — see Issue 11 in council Round 2 backlog.\"\n      mutation_boundary_exception: \"Phase 8 INVOKES the sanctioned backfill scripts (generate-description.js + backfill-graph-metadata.js). The orchestrator does not edit description.json/graph-metadata.json directly; it delegates to maintained tooling per migration-manifest M-3.3.0.0-002 fallback_operation.\"\n      step_a_graph_metadata_backfill:\n        command: |\n          # FIX-13: --active-only skips z_archive/z-future paths that the script's path-validator\n          # rejects with \"Spec folder is not under a supported specs root\" — those archive trees\n          # are outside graph-metadata backfill's traversal contract. Note: this is separate from\n          # the memory index scope. Per the archive-retention fix (commit b062b12b4), z_archive content IS\n          # indexed into the memory DB and deprioritized via ARCHIVE_MULTIPLIERS 0.1; only\n          # graph-metadata backfill's path-validator skips it.\n          node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.js --active-only 2>&1 \\\n            | tee .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.backfill-graph.log\n        timeout_seconds: 300\n        on_failure: \"warn but proceed (Phase 5.2 indexing will be partial); record failure in state log\"\n      step_b_description_backfill:\n        command: |\n          # Loop over spec folders missing description.json\n          missing_count=0\n          created_count=0\n          failed_count=0\n          while read -r spec_md; do\n            dir=$(dirname \"$spec_md\")\n            if [ ! -f \"$dir/description.json\" ]; then\n              missing_count=$((missing_count + 1))\n              if node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/dist/spec-folder/generate-description.js \\\n                \"$dir\" \"$(pwd)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n                created_count=$((created_count + 1))\n              else\n                failed_count=$((failed_count + 1))\n              fi\n            fi\n          done < <(find specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 5 -name 'spec.md' 2>/dev/null)\n          echo \"{\\\"missing\\\":$missing_count,\\\"created\\\":$created_count,\\\"failed\\\":$failed_count}\" \\\n            > .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.backfill-description.log\n        timeout_seconds: 600\n        on_failure: \"warn per-folder; aggregate failed_count for state log\"\n      report_to_dashboard: \"Phase 4 dashboard adds row 'spec-metadata-backfill: created=N, failed=M' when this sub-action runs\"\n    legacy_memory_md_detection:\n      precondition: \"always run when Phase 8 is triggered\"\n      rationale: \"v3.3 used memory/*.md files inside spec folders for continuity. v3.4 moved continuity to _memory.continuity frontmatter blocks in implementation-summary.md. The migration is NOT fully automatable — content review required per migration-manifest M-3.3.0.0-001 fallback_operation. Phase 8 detects + reports, the user runs /memory:save manually after review.\"\n      detection: |\n        find specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 6 -path '*/memory/*.md' \\\n          -not -path '*/scratch/*' -not -path '*/z_archive/*' 2>/dev/null \\\n          | tee .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.legacy-memory-files.log \\\n          | wc -l\n      action_on_findings:\n        do_not_auto_migrate: \"respecting manifest M-3.3.0.0-001 'review first' policy\"\n        write_summary_log: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.legacy-memory-files.log\"\n        recommend_to_user: |\n          # Emit at end of Phase 8:\n          if [ \"$LEGACY_MEMORY_COUNT\" -gt 0 ]; then\n            echo \"\"\n            echo \"/doctor:update detected $LEGACY_MEMORY_COUNT legacy memory/*.md files in spec packets.\"\n            echo \"These are v3.3 continuity artifacts that were superseded by _memory.continuity frontmatter in v3.4.\"\n            echo \"\"\n            echo \"RECOMMENDED MANUAL STEP: review the files listed in .doctor-update.legacy-memory-files.log,\"\n            echo \"then run \\`/memory:save\\` for each affected packet to migrate continuity into the v3.4 frontmatter format.\"\n            echo \"\"\n          fi\n\n  phase_3_snapshot_all_databases:\n    council_line: 3\n    approval: \"prompt before snapshot; include disk use estimate\"\n    condition: \"unless --no-snapshot\"\n    snapshot: \"SNAPSHOT every *.sqlite via VACUUM INTO\"\n    filename: \"<name>.pre-doctor-update.<version>.<timestamp>.bak\"\n    disk_free: \"refuse if disk free < 2x DB total\"\n    post_snapshot_hook: |\n      # Preserve original mtime on snapshot copies so age-based recovery decisions stay accurate.\n      # VACUUM INTO creates a new file with current mtime by default; reset to source mtime.\n      for src in mcp-server/database/*.sqlite mcp-server/database/*.db; do\n        [ -f \"$src\" ] || continue\n        for bak in \"$src\".pre-doctor-update.*.bak; do\n          [ -f \"$bak\" ] || continue\n          touch -r \"$src\" \"$bak\"\n        done\n      done\n    rationale: \"VACUUM INTO sets mtime to the snapshot moment, not the source's last-modified time. For age-based recovery decisions, snapshot mtime should reflect the source state being checkpointed. Council FIX-05.\"\n\n  phase_4_status_dashboard:\n    council_line: 4\n    approval: \"prompt after rendering dashboard and before selecting actions\"\n    cross_subsystem_dashboard:\n      rows: [\"context-index\", \"causal-edges\", \"skill-graph\", \"advisor\", \"deep-loop\", \"eval\"]\n      columns: [\"status\", \"age\", \"coverage\", \"recommended action\"]\n      coverage_column_rationale: \"context-index row populated by FIX-10 post_run_count_skipped output; other rows show n/a unless their tool surfaces a coverage metric\"\n\n  phase_5_dependency_order_execute:\n    council_line: 4\n    approval: \"prompt before each dependency step\"\n    dependency.order: [\"context-index\", \"causal-edges-init\", \"skill-graph\", \"advisor\", \"deep-loop-graph\", \"speckit-eval\"]\n    test_failure_injection:\n      env_var: \"SPECKIT_FAIL_STEP\"\n      scope: \"disposable workspace tests only\"\n      rule: \"Before executing each dependency step, if SPECKIT_FAIL_STEP exactly equals the dependency step name, inject a synthetic failure after snapshots and before mutating that step.\"\n      example: \"SPECKIT_FAIL_STEP=causal-edges-init\"\n      state_log_requirement: \"Record injected_failure=true, failed_step=<step>, and final_status=rolled_back when rollback is selected.\"\n    execute:\n      context-index:\n        action: \"memory_index_scan({ incremental: false, force: true })\"\n        post_run_count_skipped: |\n          # Coverage gap = on-disk spec folders (those containing spec.md) the index\n          # does not cover, computed as a set-difference (NOT total-minus-indexed: the\n          # index holds historical/phase folders, so a raw subtraction is meaningless).\n          # memory_index stores spec_folder relative to .opencode/specs and some legacy\n          # rows keep the prefix, so both sides are prefix-normalized before comparison;\n          # ln/ + external/ are excluded to mirror the memory index-scope policy. The\n          # canonical DB is resolved via shared/embeddings/profile.js (post vector-shard\n          # split it is the single context-index.sqlite; only vector shards are\n          # per-profile). The node read is cwd-independent and read-only so it never\n          # contends with the daemon's single-writer lock.\n          coverage=$(find specs -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 5 -name 'spec.md' 2>/dev/null \\\n            | sed 's#/spec.md$##' \\\n            | node -e \"\n                const fs = require('fs'), path = require('path');\n                const dir = '.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database';\n                const LOG = path.join(dir, '.doctor-update.context-index-coverage.log');\n                let Database; try { Database = require(path.resolve(dir, '../node_modules/better-sqlite3')); } catch (e) { Database = require('better-sqlite3'); }\n                const norm = (s) => String(s).replace(/^[.][/]/, '').replace(/^[.]opencode[/]specs[/]/, '').replace(/^specs[/]/, '').replace(/[/]+\\$/, '');\n                const excluded = (p) => /(^|[/])(ln|external)([/]|\\$)/.test(p);\n                const onDisk = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8').split('\\n').map(norm).filter((s) => s && !excluded(s));\n                (async () => {\n                  let dbPath;\n                  try { const m = await import(path.resolve(dir, '../../shared/dist/embeddings/profile.js')); dbPath = m.resolveActiveProfileDbPath(undefined, dir); }\n                  catch (e) { dbPath = path.join(dir, 'context-index.sqlite'); }\n                  let indexed = new Set();\n                  if (fs.existsSync(dbPath)) {\n                    const db = new Database(dbPath, { readonly: true, fileMustExist: true });\n                    indexed = new Set(db.prepare('SELECT DISTINCT spec_folder FROM memory_index WHERE spec_folder IS NOT NULL').all().map((r) => norm(r.spec_folder)));\n                    db.close();\n                  }\n                  const missing = onDisk.filter((f) => !indexed.has(f));\n                  fs.writeFileSync(LOG, JSON.stringify({ total_specs: onDisk.length, indexed: onDisk.length - missing.length, skipped: missing.length, db: path.basename(dbPath), missing: missing.slice(0, 50) }));\n                  process.stdout.write(onDisk.length + ' ' + (onDisk.length - missing.length) + ' ' + missing.length);\n                })().catch((e) => { try { fs.writeFileSync(LOG, JSON.stringify({ error: String((e && e.message) || e) })); } catch (_) {} process.stdout.write('0 0 0'); });\n              \" 2>/dev/null || echo \"0 0 0\")\n          total_specs=$(printf '%s' \"$coverage\" | cut -d' ' -f1)\n          indexed_specs=$(printf '%s' \"$coverage\" | cut -d' ' -f2)\n          skipped=$(printf '%s' \"$coverage\" | cut -d' ' -f3)\n        report_when_skipped: |\n          # Self-contained: reads the coverage log written by post_run_count_skipped,\n          # so it does not depend on shell vars surviving between steps.\n          LOG=.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/database/.doctor-update.context-index-coverage.log\n          skipped=$(node -e \"try { console.log(JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync(process.argv[1], 'utf8')).skipped || 0); } catch (e) { console.log(0); }\" \"$LOG\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\n          if [ \"${skipped:-0}\" -gt 0 ]; then\n            node -e \"\n              const d = JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync(process.argv[1], 'utf8'));\n              console.log('WARNING: context-index coverage gap detected');\n              console.log('  total spec folders found: ' + d.total_specs);\n              console.log('  indexed:                  ' + d.indexed);\n              console.log('  skipped:                  ' + d.skipped + ' (exist on disk but absent from the index)');\n              if (Array.isArray(d.missing) && d.missing.length) console.log('  e.g.: ' + d.missing.slice(0, 5).join(', ') + (d.skipped > 5 ? ' ...' : ''));\n              console.log('  run Phase 8 backfill OR /memory:save per affected packet to fix (or add the path to the index-scope exclusions if intentional)');\n            \" \"$LOG\"\n          fi\n      causal-edges-init: \"memory_causal_link(...) for high-confidence missing lineage\"\n      skill-graph: \"mk_skill_advisor.skill_graph_scan({})\"\n      advisor: \"mk_skill_advisor.advisor_rebuild({ force: true }) + mk_skill_advisor.advisor_validate({})\"\n      deep-loop-graph: \"deep_loop_graph_upsert(...)\"\n      speckit-eval: \"eval_run_ablation({})\"\n    failure:\n      council_line: 5\n      retry: \"one retry with 5-sec backoff\"\n      after_retry_failure: \"prompt retry / rollback / leave\"\n\n  phase_5_5_post_dependency_checkpoint:\n    council_line: 5\n    approval: \"auto-acknowledge unless --keep-snapshots is set\"\n    optional: true\n    detect_command: |\n      comm -13 \\\n        <(ls mcp-server/database/*.pre-doctor-update.*.bak 2>/dev/null | sed 's/\\.pre-doctor-update\\..*\\.bak$//' | sort -u) \\\n        <(ls mcp-server/database/*.sqlite mcp-server/database/*.db 2>/dev/null | sort -u)\n    checkpoint_action: |\n      # For each newly-created DB, take a \"post-bootstrap\" checkpoint snapshot.\n      for new_db in $(comm -13 ...); do\n        sqlite3 \"$new_db\" \".backup '${new_db}.post-doctor-update.${VERSION}.${TIMESTAMP}.bak'\" 2>/dev/null \\\n          || cp -p \"$new_db\" \"${new_db}.post-doctor-update.${VERSION}.${TIMESTAMP}.bak\"\n      done\n    rationale: \"Phase 3 snapshots only EXISTING DBs. On fresh install, all DBs are created during Phase 5, leaving no rollback target if Phase 7 validation fails. Phase 5.5 fills this gap. Council FIX-06.\"\n\n  phase_6_sigint_cancel_contract:\n    council_line: 6\n    SIGINT: \"set cancel flag; let current SQLite tx commit/abort; restore snapshot of in-flight DB; log cancelled by user; exit 130\"\n    settle_window: \"~5 sec per ADR-001\"\n\n  phase_7_post_run_validation:\n    council_line: 7\n    approval: \"prompt before accepting validation results when any warning exists\"\n    post.run.validation:\n      - \"existence + schema-version + row-count delta within bounds\"\n      - \"gold-battery sanity check per DB\"\n    regression: \"prompt\"\n\n  phase_9_legacy_cleanup:\n    council_line: 9\n    condition: \"user_inputs.cleanup_legacy == true\"\n    legacy: \"detect known-legacy files per migration-manifest\"\n    deletion: \"prompt-delete each; never silent\"\n\n  phase_10_state_log_unlock_cleanup:\n    council_line: 10\n    state.log: \"write .doctor-update.last-run.json with timestamps, durations, snapshot paths\"\n    release_flock: true\n    cleanup: \"prompt before deleting snapshots >30 days unless --keep-snapshots\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OUTPUT FORMAT\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noutput_format: |\n  Render phase decisions, cross-subsystem health dashboard, validation results, state log path, and STATUS.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":506,"totalLines":506,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update.yaml","time":{"start":1786890753288,"end":1786890753292}},"id":"prt_00afd1404001MwwrCL2OCiw3LA","sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","messageID":"msg_00afd0060001yDjJ6nAyu3M2YA"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1786890753407,"sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","part":{"id":"prt_00afd1208001vWXjBHjDjoLRzy","messageID":"msg_00afd0060001yDjJ6nAyu3M2YA","sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","type":"text","text":"Let me check doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml, doctor-update.yaml, and whether any fleet-wide ROUTER.md sweep exists.","time":{"start":1786890752520,"end":1786890753405}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1786890753954,"sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","part":{"id":"prt_00afd17a00014rrMi02IhBxZB6","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"789fecd89638c75c8f7e085fd8b24891109a42b9","messageID":"msg_00afd0060001yDjJ6nAyu3M2YA","sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":172189,"input":1672,"output":186,"reasoning":219,"cache":{"write":0,"read":170112}},"cost":0.0008237936}}
