{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786891015681,"sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_ET_EgVYiYZamNQVNgteIoJW2823","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Parent Skill Smart Routing Template - Root ROUTER.md Authoring\n3: description: Authoring guide for the root ROUTER.md stage-two control document: the active state maps request intent to packet-local leaf resources, and the stage1-only state delegates all routing to hub-router.json plus mode-registry.json.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"parent skill smart routing template\"\n6:   - \"root router authoring\"\n7:   - \"intent signals resource map\"\n8:   - \"leaf resource routing\"\n9:   - \"stage1-only router\"\n10: importance_tier: normal\n11: contextType: general\n12: version: 1.1.0.0\n13: router_state: active\n14: skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n15: ---\n16: \n17: # [parent-skill-name] Root Router — Two-State Authoring\n18: \n19: The parent hub's stage-two control document is first-class at the hub root as\n20: `ROUTER.md` — never at a nested path. `hub-router.json` selects a workflow mode;\n21: this document maps a request's intent to the exact packet-local leaf resources\n22: that mode loads. It declares exactly one of two states:\n23: \n24: | State | Meaning | Stage-two content |\n25: |-------|---------|-------------------|\n26: | `router_state: active` | The hub owns second-stage leaf selection | Non-empty equal-key `INTENT_SIGNALS` / `RESOURCE_MAP`; `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES` names `shared/…` control documents exempt from typed-pair checks |\n27: | `router_state: stage1-only` | The hub owns no leaf selection | Empty maps, empty stage-two default, and empty `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES`; routing delegates to `hub-router.json` plus `mode-registry.json` |\n28: \n29: Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path is either packet-qualified (`[packet]/references|assets/…`) or a shared-alias disk path (`shared/…` listed in `leaf-aliases.json`). Both convert to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the one contract boundary. Keep `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` keys aligned. Delete `FULL_INVENTORY` if the hub has no show-everything intent. A root `skill_pointer: SKILL.md` and a four-part `version` are required in both states, and the router must never coexist with a legacy `smart-routing.md`.\n30: \n31: ---\n32: \n33: ## 1. ACTIVE STATE\n34: \n35: Replace `router_state` with `active` only after a concrete leaf map exists. Every path below must resolve on disk and be registered in `leaf-manifest.json` as a typed pair.\n36: \n37: ```python\n38: # An always-loaded preamble is optional; [] keeps the default route minimal.\n39: DEFAULT_RESOURCE = []\n40: \n41: # Hub-shared control documents deliberately exempted from typed-pair checks.\n42: # Each entry must start with `shared/` and be referenced by RESOURCE_MAP below.\n43: SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES = [\"shared/references/[shared-standard].md\"]\n44: \n45: INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n46:     \"[INTENT_A]\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"[phrase a1]\", \"[phrase a2]\"]},\n47:     \"[INTENT_B]\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"[phrase b1]\", \"[phrase b2]\"]},\n48:     \"FULL_INVENTORY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"full [parent-skill-name] toolkit\", \"show the full\", \"all templates\"]},\n49: }\n50: \n51: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n52:     \"[INTENT_A]\": [\n53:         \"[packet-a]/references/[leaf-a1].md\",\n54:         \"[packet-a]/assets/[leaf-a2].md\"\n55:     ],\n56:     \"[INTENT_B]\": [\n57:         \"[packet-b]/references/[leaf-b1].md\",\n58:         \"shared/references/[shared-standard].md\"\n59:     ],\n60:     \"FULL_INVENTORY\": [\n61:         \"[packet-a]/references/[leaf-a1].md\",\n62:         \"[packet-b]/references/[leaf-b1].md\"\n63:     ],\n64: }\n65: ```\n66: \n67: ---\n68: \n69: ## 2. STAGE1-ONLY STATE\n70: \n71: A hub with no authored leaf map stays `stage1-only`: all four collections remain empty and the prose delegates routing to stage one.\n72: \n73: ```python\n74: DEFAULT_RESOURCE = []\n75: \n76: SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES = []\n77: \n78: INTENT_SIGNALS = {}\n79: \n80: RESOURCE_MAP = {}\n81: ```\n82: \n83: Promote to `active` only when the maps carry concrete, resolvable leaf paths — never placeholder intents.\n84: \n85: ---\n86: \n87: ## 3. HOW TO READ THIS\n88: \n89: - One dominant intent routes to one mode's leaf set.\n90: - Two near-tied intents (within the router's ambiguity delta) route to both leaf sets. The union is deduped by canonical pair.\n91: - No keyword match is `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK`. Confirm the target artifact and intent before loading anything.\n92: - `FULL_INVENTORY` fires only on an explicit \"show the whole toolkit\" request. Two workflow modes that share one packet directory (N-to-1 fan-out) resolve from a packet-qualified raw path to whichever mode is bound first. The fan-out twin is an exact leaf duplicate. If a hub must enumerate both twins distinctly, drive that from the manifest, not from raw router strings.\n93: \n94: ---\n95: \n96: ## 4. RELATED RESOURCES\n97: \n98: - [`parent-hub-router-schema.md`](../../references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md) - The two-axis hub router schema and the path contract these paths obey.\n99: - [`parent-skill-hub-template.md`](./parent-skill-hub-template.md) - The first-layer hub scaffold this router pairs with.\n\n(End of file - total 99 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Parent Skill Smart Routing Template - Root ROUTER.md Authoring\ndescription: Authoring guide for the root ROUTER.md stage-two control document: the active state maps request intent to packet-local leaf resources, and the stage1-only state delegates all routing to hub-router.json plus mode-registry.json.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"parent skill smart routing template\"\n  - \"root router authoring\"\n  - \"intent signals resource map\"\n  - \"leaf resource routing\"\n  - \"stage1-only router\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.1.0.0\nrouter_state: active\nskill_pointer: SKILL.md\n---\n\n# [parent-skill-name] Root Router — Two-State Authoring\n\nThe parent hub's stage-two control document is first-class at the hub root as\n`ROUTER.md` — never at a nested path. `hub-router.json` selects a workflow mode;","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/010-root-router-document-standard/.opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md","text":"---\ntitle: Parent Skill Smart Routing Template - Root ROUTER.md Authoring\ndescription: Authoring guide for the root ROUTER.md stage-two control document: the active state maps request intent to packet-local leaf resources, and the stage1-only state delegates all routing to hub-router.json plus mode-registry.json.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"parent skill smart routing template\"\n  - \"root router authoring\"\n  - \"intent signals resource map\"\n  - \"leaf resource routing\"\n  - \"stage1-only router\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.1.0.0\nrouter_state: active\nskill_pointer: SKILL.md\n---\n\n# [parent-skill-name] Root Router — Two-State Authoring\n\nThe parent hub's stage-two control document is first-class at the hub root as\n`ROUTER.md` — never at a nested path. `hub-router.json` selects a workflow mode;\nthis document maps a request's intent to the exact packet-local leaf resources\nthat mode loads. It declares exactly one of two states:\n\n| State | Meaning | Stage-two content |\n|-------|---------|-------------------|\n| `router_state: active` | The hub owns second-stage leaf selection | Non-empty equal-key `INTENT_SIGNALS` / `RESOURCE_MAP`; `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES` names `shared/…` control documents exempt from typed-pair checks |\n| `router_state: stage1-only` | The hub owns no leaf selection | Empty maps, empty stage-two default, and empty `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES`; routing delegates to `hub-router.json` plus `mode-registry.json` |\n\nEvery `RESOURCE_MAP` path is either packet-qualified (`[packet]/references|assets/…`) or a shared-alias disk path (`shared/…` listed in `leaf-aliases.json`). Both convert to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the one contract boundary. Keep `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` keys aligned. Delete `FULL_INVENTORY` if the hub has no show-everything intent. A root `skill_pointer: SKILL.md` and a four-part `version` are required in both states, and the router must never coexist with a legacy `smart-routing.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. ACTIVE STATE\n\nReplace `router_state` with `active` only after a concrete leaf map exists. Every path below must resolve on disk and be registered in `leaf-manifest.json` as a typed pair.\n\n```python\n# An always-loaded preamble is optional; [] keeps the default route minimal.\nDEFAULT_RESOURCE = []\n\n# Hub-shared control documents deliberately exempted from typed-pair checks.\n# Each entry must start with `shared/` and be referenced by RESOURCE_MAP below.\nSHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES = [\"shared/references/[shared-standard].md\"]\n\nINTENT_SIGNALS = {\n    \"[INTENT_A]\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"[phrase a1]\", \"[phrase a2]\"]},\n    \"[INTENT_B]\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"[phrase b1]\", \"[phrase b2]\"]},\n    \"FULL_INVENTORY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"full [parent-skill-name] toolkit\", \"show the full\", \"all templates\"]},\n}\n\nRESOURCE_MAP = {\n    \"[INTENT_A]\": [\n        \"[packet-a]/references/[leaf-a1].md\",\n        \"[packet-a]/assets/[leaf-a2].md\"\n    ],\n    \"[INTENT_B]\": [\n        \"[packet-b]/references/[leaf-b1].md\",\n        \"shared/references/[shared-standard].md\"\n    ],\n    \"FULL_INVENTORY\": [\n        \"[packet-a]/references/[leaf-a1].md\",\n        \"[packet-b]/references/[leaf-b1].md\"\n    ],\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. STAGE1-ONLY STATE\n\nA hub with no authored leaf map stays `stage1-only`: all four collections remain empty and the prose delegates routing to stage one.\n\n```python\nDEFAULT_RESOURCE = []\n\nSHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES = []\n\nINTENT_SIGNALS = {}\n\nRESOURCE_MAP = {}\n```\n\nPromote to `active` only when the maps carry concrete, resolvable leaf paths — never placeholder intents.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW TO READ THIS\n\n- One dominant intent routes to one mode's leaf set.\n- Two near-tied intents (within the router's ambiguity delta) route to both leaf sets. The union is deduped by canonical pair.\n- No keyword match is `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK`. Confirm the target artifact and intent before loading anything.\n- `FULL_INVENTORY` fires only on an explicit \"show the whole toolkit\" request. Two workflow modes that share one packet directory (N-to-1 fan-out) resolve from a packet-qualified raw path to whichever mode is bound first. The fan-out twin is an exact leaf duplicate. If a hub must enumerate both twins distinctly, drive that from the manifest, not from raw router strings.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [`parent-hub-router-schema.md`](../../references/parent-skill/parent-hub-router-schema.md) - The two-axis hub router schema and the path contract these paths obey.\n- [`parent-skill-hub-template.md`](./parent-skill-hub-template.md) - The first-layer hub scaffold this router pairs with.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":99,"totalLines":99,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md","time":{"start":1786891015672,"end":1786891015680}},"id":"prt_00b011528001UZQ7hd58EjWUji","sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","messageID":"msg_00b0104bd001381bONSlXpXhJG"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1786891015769,"sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","part":{"id":"prt_00b0112b2001qLpz7Y13PXa2IB","messageID":"msg_00b0104bd001381bONSlXpXhJG","sessionID":"ses_ff5086a9cffeOVVmWhMNGVn4l3","type":"text","text":"Iteration 4: classify the sk-create-skill smart-routing hits. I already have most context. Let me read the parent-skill-hub-router-template.json and parent-skill-smart-routing-template.md (the key files) plus the parent-skill-hub-template.md relevant section.","time":{"start":1786891014834,"end":1786891015767}}}
